  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607196600: Bounded PostgreSQL named portals

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

The database provider exposes named portal Bind, bounded Fetch and explicit
Close operations. Portal and statement names are independently validated, and
Bind parameters pass through the typed bounded parameter validator. Fetch
requires a positive row limit no greater than 1024 and cannot request an
unbounded result.

Each Fetch must produce exactly one of PortalSuspended or CommandComplete,
followed by ReadyForQuery. Duplicate or conflicting terminal tags, malformed
frames and missing transaction status fail closed. Portals are used inside an
explicit transaction and never become ambient connection or cursor handles;
all activity remains on the existing affine TLS database channel.

## Evidence

Released PostgreSQL 14.19 qualification prepares
`select generate_series(1,3)`, begins a transaction, binds named portal `page`,
fetches two rows and requires PortalSuspended, fetches the remaining row and
requires CommandComplete, explicitly closes the portal, commits, closes the
statement and verifies all transport handles are released.

This closes the bounded named cursor slice. Batch/pipeline execution, COPY,
pooling, credential/certificate rotation, compatibility matrices and soak
remain open.")))
